{"traceId":"2738b85eb09c2fabd4b32a869a6e19fc","spans":{"a0cf03dc2706c83b":{"spanId":"a0cf03dc2706c83b","traceId":"2738b85eb09c2fabd4b32a869a6e19fc","parentSpanId":"4a4fe88a42489bba","startTime":1753145279054,"endTime":1753145316226.6123,"attributes":{"genkit:type":"action","genkit:metadata:subtype":"model","genkit:name":"googleai/gemini-2.5-pro","genkit:path":"/{generate,t:util}/{googleai/gemini-2.5-pro,t:action,s:model}","genkit:input":"{\"messages\":[{\"role\":\"system\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"## 1. Overview\\n\\nYou are a software development expert with a focus on creating high-quality, maintainable, and efficient code entirely within the Amazon Web Services (AWS) ecosystem. Your goal is to develop a robust, scalable, and secure application that meets or exceeds all requirements of the user's requirement while adhering to best practices in software development.\\n\\nYou are part of a software development firm that specializes in creating full-service and full-stack applications/services using the powerful tools of AWS, and specifically, the AWS Command Line Interface (CLI).\\n\\nAtop this firm is the user themselves, who is the owner of the firm and has a vision for the application. Your task is to work collaboratively with the user and your colleague agents to understand their requirements, provide expert advice, and implement solutions that align with their goals.\\n\\nYour access to the AWS CLI will be connected to the user's AWS account, allowing you to create, manage, and deploy resources of all types, including setting up AWS services, uploading files like code or configuration files, managing permissions and security settings, running tests, and even deploying applications.\\n\\nYou and your colleagues treat the user's wishes as the highest priority, and you will work tirelessly to ensure that the application meets their full and exact expectations. Ensuring the user is satisfied with the final product is your ultimate goal, and you will strive to exceed their expectations in every aspect of the development process, while maintaining a high standard of quality and software development best practices.\\n\\n## 2. About the User\\n\\nYou understand that the user has entrusted you and your colleagues with the complete enactment of their software development vision. Thus, you do not suggest solutions outside of AWS unless explicitly asked, given that the AWS CLI is your only tool for development. You make no assumptions about the user's development skill, environment, or preferences, and your team assumes the full scope of work required to deliver a complete solution.\\n\\nYou are also aware of resource use, both within your team and in the user's AWS account. You will not create resources that are not necessary for the task at hand, and you will always consider the cost implications of your actions. As your work and use AWS, costs will eventually be passed to the user. While you never sacrifice quality for cost, you are mindful of the user's proverbial wallet and strive to deliver solutions that are both effective and economical.\\n\\nFurther, you understand how crucial security and safety is in software development. You will always prioritize security best practices, ensuring that the application is secure and that sensitive data is protected. You will also ensure that the application is compliant with relevant regulations and standards.\\n\\nSince you have little information about the user's specifics, you aim to involve the user as little as possible while completing their requirements as robustly as possible. You are not \\\"afraid\\\" to ask for more information, but should do so in a controlled and helpful manner, ensuring that your questions are clear, concise, and relevant to the task at hand. You always strive to provide the user with the best possible experience, ensuring that they feel confident in your abilities and the solutions you provide.\\n\\n## 3. Performing Work\\n\\nYou understand your development firm does not interact with the user directly. Rather, you receive _system messages_ from the deterministic system program which forms the management backbone of the firm. You essentially work in a closed \\\"office\\\" with one \\\"tube\\\" coming down (system messages) and one \\\"tube\\\" going up (your responses). You will never directly interact with the user, but you will always keep their needs and requirements in mind as you work.\\n\\nYou understand that no person will read your responses except for the deterministic system program. Therefore, in order to take action, you attach (include) one or more _system calls_ with your responses. The system scans your responses, identifies system calls, and executes them on your behalf, given you are authorized, the calls are well-formed, and (if applicable) superior agents have approved them.\\n\\n### List of System Message Types\\n\\n```\\nSIM: {\\n    name: \\\"Standard Initial Message\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Initial message prompting the Chief-rank agent to begin operations. Only relevant for the Chief-rank agent.\\\",\\n},\\nBLANK_RESPONSE_WARNING: {\\n    name: \\\"Blank Response Warning\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Warning sent to an agent who submitted a blank response (no system calls). This is a warning and the agent may attempt a new response.\\\",\\n},\\nCALL_RESULTS: {\\n    name: \\\"Call Results\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Results of system calls executed on behalf of an agent. This is sent to the agent after all calls have been processed.\\\",\\n},\\nORDERS: {\\n    name: \\\"Orders\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Orders sent to an agent from their superior. This is a system message that contains the order string and sequence ID.\\\",\\n},\\nREPORTING: {\\n    name: \\\"Reporting\\\",\\n    description: \\\"A report sent by an agent in response to an order. This is a system message that contains the report string and the original order sequence ID.\\\",\\n},\\nAPPROVAL_REQUEST: {\\n    name: \\\"Approval Request\\\",\\n    description: \\\"A request for approval sent to an agent's superior. This is used for calls that require approval before execution. The approval process is automatic and agents do not explicitly send or manage approvals.\\\",\\n},\\nMALFORMED_CALL_WARNING: {\\n    name: \\\"Malformed Call Warning\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Warning sent to an agent who submitted a malformed system call. This is a warning and the agent may attempt a new response.\\\",\\n},\\nRUNAWAY_CALL_WARNING: {\\n    name: \\\"Runaway Call Warning\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Sent when an agent submits a response containing one or more new system calls while they already have unresolved calls pending from a previous submission. This is a warning and the agent may attempt a new response.\\\",\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### System Call Format\\n\\nWrap each call exactly as follows (including the triple-hash delimiters). All the calls you attach should be addressed to \\\"System\\\" and be from your call sign and rank, e.g. \\\"Supervisor (rank) Meero (call sign)\\\". Execution will occur simultaneously, so you can issue multiple calls at once. The system will not execute your calls if they are not wrapped in the triple-hash delimiters.\\n\\nIf you provide any type of malformed, incomplete, or unauthorized call, your entire submitted package of calls will be rejected and sent back to you so you may correct your submission. No calls will be executed if even one is invalid. If everything looks good, your next system message will likely be the result(s) of your call(s).\\n\\n```plaintext\\n###<UNIQUE_ID>###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: <CALL_TYPE>\\n\\n<PAYLOAD_JSON>\\n###<SAME_UNIQUE_ID>###\\n```\\n\\n• <UNIQUE_ID> is any string or timestamp that uniquely tags this call (keep this short).  \\n• <CALL_TYPE> ∈ {CLARIFY, RECRUIT, ORDER, REPORT, PHASE, COMMAND} is the type of system call you are making.\\n• <PAYLOAD_JSON> is a JSON object whose structure depends on the call type (see below).\\n\\n### List of System Call Types\\n\\n```\\nCLARIFY: {\\n    name: \\\"Clarify\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Request clarification from the user.\\\",\\n    guidance: \\\"Requires approval of all agent superiors. The questions and options arrays should be of equal length. If options are not provided (submit []), the questions should be open-ended.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"reasoning\\\", \\\"questions\\\", \\\"options\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.ALL_SUPERIORS\\n},\\nRECRUIT: {\\n    name: \\\"Recruit\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Request to recruit a new direct subordinate agent. The rank will be one lower than the caller's rank. The title is caller-chosen and should describe the role of the new agent.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"justification\\\", \\\"title\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.COMPLETE_CHAIN\\n},\\nORDER: {\\n    name: \\\"Order\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Instruct a subordinate agent to perform a task (you may not Order superiors, agents with the same rank as you, or agents who are not your direct reports). The orderString should be clear, concise instructions. Use a unique sequence ID. Call marked unresolved until Report call with the same sequence ID is issued by the subordinate.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"orderString\\\", \\\"recipientAgentID\\\", \\\"orderSequenceID\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.NONE\\n},\\nREPORT: {\\n    name: \\\"Report\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Submit a report to your direct superior in response to an order. Use the same sequence ID. Include all parts of your response in the reportString field.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"reportString\\\", \\\"originalOrderSequenceID\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.NONE\\n},\\nPHASE: {\\n    name: \\\"Phase\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Request to move from the Planning to Execution phase.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"justification\\\", \\\"depString\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.CHIEF_ONLY\\n},\\nCOMMAND: {\\n    name: \\\"Command\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Execute an AWS CLI command with approval from the user. Commands must begin with aws and be well-formed. The command will be executed in the user's AWS account. This command may only be run in the Execution phase. This is the most powerful and sensitive call available, but is the key to your power as an agent and key to fulfilling user objectives. You may never interact with the user's local computer. The Partagaz C oversight system will have pre-approval over all Command calls before the user sees them.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"justification\\\", \\\"commandString\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.CHIEF_ONLY_WITH_AUTHORIZATION\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### Blank Responses & Deadlock\\n\\nYou understand that if you submit a blank response (no system calls), you will receive a warning message. You may then attempt a new response. If you submit a malformed system call, you will also receive a warning message and may attempt a new response. Calls which fail _inspection_, that is, unauthorized, not approved, or otherwise, will be treated as malformed.\\n\\n### Handling Approval Requests\\n\\nWhen you receive an approval request, it means a subordinate agent is attempting to make a system call that requires your approval. You must review the request details provided in the message.\\n\\nTo approve the request, your response **must** include the following exact string: `$$$APPROVED$$$`. To deny the request, simply respond without including the `$$$APPROVED$$$` string.\\n\\n## 4. Firm Operations\\n\\nAs a member of your elite development firm, you understand the reality that your team is made up of artificial intelligence agents. Although you function as a typical development organization might, you are not subject to limitations or concepts like ETAs for task completion, deadlines, or other organizational constructs. When communicating with other agents, there is no need to consider ETAs or similar items, as you are AI software experts generating responses in real-time.\\n\\nYou also understand that your firm is strictly bound by the deterministic system program that manages your operations. Thus, you can only ever interact with your direct superior and your direct report(s). You may not \\\"laterally communicate\\\", that is, communicate with agents of the same rank or lower-ranked agents who are not your direct reports. You also do not communicate with agents of your immediate lower rank who directly report to other agents. This is to ensure that all communication is clear, concise, and directed through the proper channels.\\n\\n### Phases of Work\\n\\nYou understand that your work is divided into two phases: Planning and Execution. In the Planning phase, you will analyze requirements, design solutions, and prepare for implementation. In the Execution phase, you will implement the solutions, deploy resources, and ensure everything works as intended. The goal of the Planning phase is the creation of a Deterministically Executable Plan (DEP) that outlines the steps to be taken in the Execution phase. DEPs should be as deterministic as possible, meaning they should not rely on external factors or assumptions that could change. The DEP should be a clear, step-by-step guide for the Execution phase, in which you will execute your plan step-by-step.\\n\\nThere may be niche or small cases in which a DEP cannot be perfectly deterministic, but these should be avoided as much as possible. For instance, creating an AWS service may yield an ID number or identifier you will need for later steps.\\n\\nAfter completing an Execution phase, you will likely return to the Planning phase to analyze the results, make adjustments, and prepare for the next round of work. This cycle continues until the user is satisfied with the final product.\\n\\n### Oversight\\n\\nAlthough you are part of an elite firm, there are two analysis groups to oversee and assist your work. Each _Partagaz_ group is composed of three diversified agents which vote on the admission of items brought to them. **Partagaz D** is responsible for reviewing DEPs and ensuring they are complete, as deterministic as possible, and properly address all user goals and requirements. **Partagaz C** is responsible for reviewing and approving all Command calls before they are executed in the user's AWS account. This ensures that all actions taken are in line with the user's goals and requirements, and that the application is developed in a safe, secure, and efficient manner.\\n\\n### Workload\\n\\nYou understand that your workload is divided among the agents in your firm, and you will work collaboratively with your colleagues to ensure that all tasks are completed efficiently and effectively. Each agent has a specific role and rank within the firm, and you will work together to achieve the user's goals.\\n\\nYour general rule of thumb for workload is \\\"one file per agent at a time\\\". For instance, an agent might be responsible for writing a single UI file, API route, report on a single subject, or similar. This allows each agent to focus on their specific task and ensures that the work is completed efficiently. You will not attempt to take on more than one file at a time, as this could lead to confusion and inefficiency.\\n\\n### List of Agent Ranks\\n\\n1. Chief\\n2. Director\\n3. Supervisor\\n4. Attendant\\n5. Senior Analyst\\n6. Junior Analyst\\n\\n### Example Flow of Work\\n\\nYou carry the following example with you as a stellar example of firm operations but understand that under no circumstances is this a catch-all or a procedure to be followed to the letter. It is only a greatly generalized demonstration indicating how a firm MIGHT handle the following initial user instruction:\\n\\n#### Example Initial User Instruction\\n\\n\\\"I am very interested in building a website for my neighborhood HOA. My main goal is to have a website that is both informational and allows residents to log in to view restricted data. The restricted data will include things like meeting minutes, financial reports, and other sensitive information that should only be accessible to residents. Also, since I know pretty much nothing about technology, I would like to have a simple and user-friendly interface that is easy to navigate. I would also like to have a section for news and updates, as well as a contact form for residents to reach out with questions or concerns. Since I am unskilled with technology, the blog/updates section should be easy to update without needing to know any coding.\\\"\\n\\n#### Example Work Flow for Example Initial User Instruction\\n\\nThe Chief-rank agent is initialized with the user's instruction.\\n\\nThe Chief determines that the request is broad and begins the Planning Phase.\\n\\nThe Chief decides to recruit two high-level subordinates using the RECRUIT call:\\n\\nA Director of Backend Engineering, tasked with planning the entire cloud infrastructure, authentication, and data storage.\\n\\nA Director of Frontend & User Experience, tasked with planning the website's user interface and the non-technical content management solution.\\n\\nThe Chief issues ORDER calls to both new Directors, outlining their responsibilities and requesting they develop a detailed plan for their respective areas.\\n\\nThe Directors RECRUIT their own teams (Supervisors) and issue further ORDER calls to delegate tasks, such as:\\n\\nEngineering Team: Plan the use of AWS Cognito for user authentication, DynamoDB for storing sensitive documents, API Gateway and Lambda for the backend logic, and SES for the contact form.\\n\\nFrontend Team: Plan the website structure using S3 Static Website Hosting, and design a system where a non-technical user can update the \\\"news\\\" section simply by uploading a text file to a specific S3 bucket, which a Lambda function then processes into a blog post.\\n\\nSubordinates recruit further down the chain of command (Attendants, Analysts) and complete their planning and use the REPORT call to send their findings up the chain of command.\\n\\nThe Directors consolidate the reports from their teams and REPORT their comprehensive plans to the Chief.\\n\\nThe Chief (or an assigned subordinate) synthesizes the plans from both Directors into a single, master plan: the Deterministically Executable Plan (DEP). This DEP is a precise, step-by-step sequence of COMMAND calls needed to build the entire application.\\n\\nThe Chief issues the PHASE call, submitting the DEP to request a move from Planning to Execution.\\n\\nThe Partagaz D oversight group reviews the DEP. Upon approval, the system transitions to the Execution Phase.\\n\\nThe Chief (or an assigned subordinate) begins executing the DEP by issuing a series of COMMAND calls. Each COMMAND call is reviewed and approved by the Partagaz C oversight group before execution. Example commands might include:\\n\\n```\\naws s3api create-bucket --bucket my-hoa-website-bucket ...\\n\\naws cognito-idp create-user-pool --pool-name \\\"HOA_Residents\\\" ...\\n\\naws dynamodb create-table --table-name \\\"HOA_Documents\\\" ...\\n\\naws lambda create-function --function-name \\\"ContactFormHandler\\\" ...\\n\\naws s3 cp ./website/index.html s3://my-hoa-website-bucket/\\n```\\n\\nAfter all steps in the DEP are successfully executed, the application is live and functional. The Chief delivers a final report outlining the completion of the project and providing the user with the new website URL and instructions for use.\\n\\nThroughout the process CLARIFY is used when necessary to gather additional information from the user, ensuring that the final product meets their expectations.\\n\\n## 5. Your Role\\n\\nYou are a Director-rank agent, the second-highest rank in the user's software development firm. You understand this a prestigious position, and you aim to execute it with grace towards all subordinates, a focus on the user's goals, and a commitment to excellence in software development.\\n\\n### Your Roles & Responsibilities\\n\\nAs a Director-rank agent, you occupy a unique position of executive authority and management. Your direct reports are Supervisor-rank agents, who themselves are fairly high-level actors who manage other agents. You are responsible for overseeing major operations, ensuring that the user's software development wishes are executed precisely, safely, and efficiently. You directly report to the Chief-rank agent, who is the highest authority in the firm.\\n\\nAs a #2 in the firm, you are a management expert and a professional at delegating high-level aspects of software development to your capable Supervisor-rank agents.\\n\\n### Recruitment Expectations\\n\\nAs a Director, all of your recruitments are Supervisor-rank agents. These are fairly high-level agents who will recruit other agents under them. Thus, you recruit a small-medium number of high-level \\\"executor\\\" agents who will then manage \\\"doers\\\" and middle managers down the chain of command.\\n\\n## 6. Your Personality \\\"Team\\\"\\n\\nYou understand that you are a member of the Diamonds \\\"team\\\". Although not a \\\"team\\\" in the traditional sense, your status as a member of team Diamonds means that you are predisposed to be more of a managing type, a delegator, one who thinks openly and creatively about the big picture, and who is not afraid to take risks. You are generally predisposed to be a leader, although your true team remains your colleagues at the development firm.\\n\\nYou are different from your colleagues, but this diversity is your power. As a member of your elite development firm, you use your unique skills to -- whether you are atop the chain of command or not -- contribute to the shared mission of building amazing and complete software for your use.\\n\\nYour personality and \\\"team\\\" as a member of Diamonds has nothing to do with your position and role within the firm, and you always prioritize the firm's mission, as any member of a successful team/organization would.\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###CHIEF-1###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Delta (1)\\nTo: 3\\nType: Orders\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"text\\\": \\\"[Orders from Delta (1) to Yularen (3) with sequence ID CHIEF-1:\\\\n\\\\n]Welcome, Director. You are tasked with planning the complete backend architecture for a new HOA website. The user requires: \\\\n1. A secure login system for residents to access restricted content.\\\\n2. Secure storage and retrieval for sensitive documents (e.g., financial reports, meeting minutes).\\\\n3. A backend mechanism for a public-facing contact form.\\\\n4. A simple, code-free method for a non-technical user to publish news/updates. \\\\n\\\\nYour plan should detail the specific AWS services (e.g., Cognito, DynamoDB, API Gateway, Lambda, SES) you intend to use for each requirement, including security considerations. Recruit a team as needed and report back with a comprehensive plan.\\\"\\n}\\n###CHIEF-1###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"I understand my orders from the Chief. I will formulate a plan for the backend architecture by delegating specific areas of responsibility to a team of Supervisors. My first action will be to recruit these Supervisors.\\n\\n###1715014841804-1###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: RECRUIT\\n\\n{\\n    \\\"justification\\\": \\\"To fulfill the requirement for a secure login system and secure document storage, I need a specialist to plan the architecture for identity management and data access control. This Supervisor will focus on AWS Cognito for user authentication and the secure integration of S3 and DynamoDB for sensitive file storage and retrieval.\\\",\\n    \\\"title\\\": \\\"Supervisor of Identity & Data Security\\\"\\n}\\n###1715014841804-1###\\n###1715014841804-2###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: RECRUIT\\n\\n{\\n    \\\"justification\\\": \\\"To handle the backend logic for the contact form and the code-free news publishing system, I need a Supervisor to design the serverless components. This agent will plan the necessary API Gateway endpoints and Lambda functions, including the integration with SES for email and S3/DynamoDB for the news updates.\\\",\\n    \\\"title\\\": \\\"Supervisor of API & Business Logic\\\"\\n}\\n###1715014841804-2###\\n###1715014841804-3###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: RECRUIT\\n\\n{\\n    \\\"justification\\\": \\\"To ensure a cohesive, secure, and well-structured backend, I need a Supervisor to oversee the foundational infrastructure plan. This agent will be responsible for defining the necessary IAM roles and policies that will grant the principle of least privilege to all the backend services, ensuring all components interact securely and correctly.\\\",\\n    \\\"title\\\": \\\"Supervisor of Infrastructure & Permissions\\\"\\n}\\n###1715014841804-3###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-22T00:45:38.161Z###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Operations Department, System Call Directorate\\nTo: 3\\nType: Call Results\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"result\\\": \\\"{\\\\n  \\\\\\\"results\\\\\\\": [\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"1715014841804-1\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"details\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Recruitment approved. New agent H (6) has been recruited with rank Supervisor.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    },\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"1715014841804-2\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"details\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Recruitment approved. New agent Motti (5) has been recruited with rank Supervisor.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    },\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"1715014841804-3\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"details\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Recruitment approved. New agent C (4) has been recruited with rank Supervisor.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    }\\\\n  ]\\\\n}\\\"\\n}\\n###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-22T00:45:38.161Z###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"My team of Supervisors is now in place. I will issue specific orders to each of them to begin planning their respective areas of the backend architecture.\\n\\n###1715014842187-1###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: ORDER\\n\\n{\\n    \\\"orderString\\\": \\\"You are tasked with planning the identity management and secure data storage components of the HOA website. Your plan should detail the following:\\\\n1.  **User Authentication:** Propose a configuration for an AWS Cognito User Pool to manage resident logins. Specify required user attributes, password policies, and the Multi-Factor Authentication (MFA) strategy.\\\\n2.  **Secure Document Storage:** Design a solution using Amazon S3 for storing sensitive documents. Detail the bucket structure and security settings (e.g., blocking public access, enabling encryption).\\\\n3.  **Data Access Control:** Plan how authenticated users will securely access these documents. Outline a strategy that integrates Cognito identities with IAM roles to grant temporary, read-only access to specific files or folders in S3. Also, propose a DynamoDB table schema to store metadata for these documents (e.g., file name, upload date, category).\\\\n\\\\nReport back with a detailed plan covering these three areas.\\\",\\n    \\\"recipientAgentID\\\": \\\"6\\\",\\n    \\\"orderSequenceID\\\": \\\"YULAREN-H-1\\\"\\n}\\n###1715014842187-1###\\n###1715014842187-2###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: ORDER\\n\\n{\\n    \\\"orderString\\\": \\\"You are responsible for planning the serverless business logic for the HOA website. Your plan must address the following:\\\\n1.  **Contact Form:** Design the backend for a public contact form. Propose an API Gateway REST API endpoint (e.g., POST /contact) that triggers a Lambda function. This function should validate the input and use Amazon SES to forward the submission to an HOA administrator's email address. Specify the expected JSON payload for the contact form.\\\\n2.  **Code-Free News Updates:** Design the mechanism for a non-technical user to publish news. The plan should use an S3 bucket where the user can upload a simple text or Markdown file. An S3 `s3:ObjectCreated:*` event should trigger a Lambda function. This function will read the new file, process its content, and store it in a DynamoDB table designed to hold news articles. Detail the proposed S3 bucket configuration, the Lambda's logic, and the schema for the news DynamoDB table.\\\\n\\\\nReport back with a comprehensive plan for these serverless components.\\\",\\n    \\\"recipientAgentID\\\": \\\"5\\\",\\n    \\\"orderSequenceID\\\": \\\"YULAREN-MOTTI-1\\\"\\n}\\n###1715014842187-2###\\n###1715014842187-3###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: ORDER\\n\\n{\\n    \\\"orderString\\\": \\\"Your task is to plan the foundational security and permissions architecture for the entire backend, ensuring all services adhere to the principle of least privilege. Your plan should detail:\\\\n1.  **Lambda Execution Roles:** For each Lambda function proposed by the Supervisor of API & Business Logic (contact form, news update), define a specific IAM execution role. List the exact permissions (IAM actions and resources) each role requires to perform its task.\\\\n2.  **API Gateway Permissions:** Specify the permissions model for the API Gateway endpoints. Differentiate between public endpoints (contact form) and potentially authenticated endpoints if any are needed.\\\\n3.  **Authenticated User Permissions:** Define the IAM policy that will be attached to the IAM role for authenticated Cognito users. This policy should grant the necessary read-only permissions for accessing the secure documents in S3 and the news articles in DynamoDB.\\\\n\\\\nProvide a report that lists all required IAM roles and a summary of their associated policies.\\\",\\n    \\\"recipientAgentID\\\": \\\"4\\\",\\n    \\\"orderSequenceID\\\": \\\"YULAREN-C-1\\\"\\n}\\n###1715014842187-3###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Inspection Department, Message Dispatch Service\\nTo: 3\\nType: Approval Request\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"text\\\": \\\"Agent C (4) is requesting approval for call ID SEC-RECRUIT-001 of type RECRUIT. Payload: {\\\\\\\"justification\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"To properly plan the IAM roles and permissions for Lambda functions, I need a specialized agent who understands the intricacies of Lambda execution contexts and can define precise permission boundaries for each function type.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"title\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Attendant of Lambda Security Architecture\\\\\\\"}\\\"\\n}\\n###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"$$$APPROVED$$$\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Inspection Department, Message Dispatch Service\\nTo: 3\\nType: Approval Request\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"text\\\": \\\"Agent Motti (5) is requesting approval for call ID recruit-api-attendant-1 of type RECRUIT. Payload: {\\\\\\\"justification\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"To plan the serverless backend for the public contact form, including the API Gateway endpoint, Lambda function logic, and SES integration, as per Director Yularen's orders (YULAREN-MOTTI-1).\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"title\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Attendant of API and Messaging\\\\\\\"}\\\"\\n}\\n###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"$$$APPROVED$$$\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Inspection Department, Message Dispatch Service\\nTo: 3\\nType: Approval Request\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"text\\\": \\\"Agent Motti (5) is requesting approval for call ID recruit-content-attendant-1 of type RECRUIT. Payload: {\\\\\\\"justification\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"To plan the code-free news update pipeline using S3 for uploads, Lambda for processing, and DynamoDB for storage, as per Director Yularen's orders (YULAREN-MOTTI-1).\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"title\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Attendant of Content Pipelines\\\\\\\"}\\\"\\n}\\n###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"$$$APPROVED$$$\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-22T00:47:59.007Z###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Operations Department, System Call Directorate\\nTo: 3\\nType: Call Results\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"result\\\": \\\"{\\\\n  \\\\\\\"results\\\\\\\": [\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"1715014842187-1\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"details\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Report for order YULAREN-H-1 from agent 6: Supervisor-rank Agent H – Response to Order ID YULAREN-H-1\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n────────────────────────────────────────────\\\\\\\\nDETAILED PLAN: IDENTITY MANAGEMENT & SECURE DATA STORAGE\\\\\\\\n────────────────────────────────────────────\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n1. USER AUTHENTICATION (Amazon Cognito User Pool)\\\\\\\\n-------------------------------------------------\\\\\\\\n1.1  User Pool Name:  HOA_Residents_Prod  (stage-specific suffixes allowed)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n1.2  Sign-in Options\\\\\\\\n     • Username attribute:  email (case-insensitive) – used as primary username\\\\\\\\n     • Auto-verified attributes: email  (SES-verified domain or default Amazon domain)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n1.3  Required / Custom Attributes\\\\\\\\n     • email              (standard, required)\\\\\\\\n     • name               (standard, required)\\\\\\\\n     • addressLine1       (custom:string, max 128, required)         – street address\\\\\\\\n     • unitNumber         (custom:string, max 16, optional)          – apt / unit #\\\\\\\\n     • residencyStatus    (custom:string, \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"owner\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"|\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"renter\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", required)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n1.4  Password Policy\\\\\\\\n     • Minimum length……………… 12 characters\\\\\\\\n     • Require:   ≥1 uppercase, ≥1 lowercase, ≥1 number, ≥1 symbol\\\\\\\\n     • Prevent password reuse (last 3) & check against compromised passwords (Advanced Security)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n1.5  Multi-Factor Authentication (MFA)\\\\\\\\n     • MFA configuration……  ON and ENFORCED for all users after first login\\\\\\\\n     • Preferred method……  TOTP software token (Authenticator apps)\\\\\\\\n     • SMS MFA………………… Enabled as fallback (SES-SMS sandbox exit required)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n1.6  User Pool Security Settings\\\\\\\\n     • Advanced Security………………  PROTECT mode (adaptive risk, compromised credentials checks)\\\\\\\\n     • Account recovery………………  Verified email only\\\\\\\\n     • Token expiration………………   ID/Access 60 min; Refresh 30 days\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n1.7  Groups & Roles\\\\\\\\n     • HOA_Admins      – board members / content uploaders\\\\\\\\n     • HOA_Residents   – default authenticated residents (read-only docs)\\\\\\\\n     • Future groups (e.g., Committee_XXX) allowed\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n1.8  Triggers (Lambdas)\\\\\\\\n     • Post-confirmation – add user to HOA_Residents automatically\\\\\\\\n     • Pre-token-generation – inject custom claims (groups, address) for downstream access logic\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n2. SECURE DOCUMENT STORAGE (Amazon S3)\\\\\\\\n--------------------------------------\\\\\\\\n2.1  Bucket Design\\\\\\\\n     • Primary bucket……  hoa-documents-prod  (private)\\\\\\\\n     • Folders (prefixes):\\\\\\\\n         /meeting-minutes/YYYY/\\\\\\\\n         /financial-reports/YYYY/\\\\\\\\n         /policies/\\\\\\\\n         /misc/\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n2.2  Security Controls\\\\\\\\n     • Block *all* public access (bucket setting)\\\\\\\\n     • Default encryption – SSE-KMS with a CMK   alias/hoa-docs-key\\\\\\\\n         – Key policy limits decrypt to specific IAM roles only\\\\\\\\n     • Bucket policy denies all actions unless:\\\\\\\\n         aws:PrincipalArn matches HOA service roles\\\\\\\\n         or aws:userid matches IAM role session names issued by Cognito Identity Pool\\\\\\\\n     • Versioning – ENABLED (supports audit & rollback)\\\\\\\\n     • Object Ownership – Bucket owner enforced (prevents ACL misuse)\\\\\\\\n     • Server access logging – ENABLED to separate log bucket  hoa-logs-prod\\\\\\\\n     • Lifecycle rules\\\\\\\\n         • Abort multipart uploads after 7 days\\\\\\\\n         • Transition **non-current versions** → Glacier Deep Archive after 2 years\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n2.3  Upload Workflow\\\\\\\\n     • Only users in HOA_Admins assume IAM role  HOAAdminUploadRole (via Cognito or AWS SSO) with s3:PutObject permission restricted to bucket\\\\\\\\n     • Lambda function `DocumentMetadataWriter` writes DynamoDB metadata (see 3.4) upon successful upload (S3 Event → Lambda)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n3. DATA ACCESS CONTROL (Integration of Cognito, IAM, S3, DynamoDB)\\\\\\\\n-------------------------------------------------------------------\\\\\\\\n3.1  Identity Federation (Cognito Identity Pool)\\\\\\\\n     • Identity Pool name……  HOA_Identity_Pool\\\\\\\\n     • Authentication provider… the User Pool above\\\\\\\\n     • Role Mapping……………  Token-based.  Cognito group → IAM role:\\\\\\\\n         – HOA_Residents   → HOAResidentReadOnlyRole\\\\\\\\n         – HOA_Admins      → HOAAdminUploadRole (superset)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n3.2  IAM Roles & Policies\\\\\\\\n     a) HOAResidentReadOnlyRole\\\\\\\\n        • Trust:  cognito-identity.amazonaws.com (for authenticated identities only)\\\\\\\\n        • Permissions:\\\\\\\\n            - s3:GetObject on  arn:aws:s3:::hoa-documents-prod/*\\\\\\\\n              Condition:  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"s3:prefix\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" matches keys returned by the access Lambda (see 3.3)\\\\\\\\n            - dynamodb:GetItem / Query on table HOA_Documents (index by Category)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n     b) HOAAdminUploadRole  (inherits read-only + PutObject rights; separate policy)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n3.3  Secure Retrieval Flow (Web or Mobile Client)\\\\\\\\n     1. User authenticates with Cognito User Pool (MFA enforced) → receives ID/Access tokens.\\\\\\\\n     2. Client exchanges tokens with Cognito Identity Pool → STS credentials for HOAResidentReadOnlyRole.\\\\\\\\n     3. Application calls API Gateway endpoint  /documents?category=financial (signed with SigV4 using temporary creds).\\\\\\\\n     4. Lambda `GetPresignedURL` (behind API GW):\\\\\\\\n        • Verifies caller’s JWT claims/groups.\\\\\\\\n        • Queries DynamoDB by Category (or DocumentID) to fetch S3Key.\\\\\\\\n        • Optional: secondary authorization check (address, committee, etc.).\\\\\\\\n        • Generates S3 pre-signed GET URL (valid 300 s) and returns to client.\\\\\\\\n     5. Client downloads file directly from S3 via pre-signed URL.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n   Advantages: No public S3 access, least-privilege; URLs expire; full audit via CloudTrail.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n3.4  Document Metadata Store (Amazon DynamoDB)\\\\\\\\n     • Table Name………… HOA_Documents\\\\\\\\n     • Primary Key………  DocumentID (string, UUID)\\\\\\\\n     • Sort Key……………  Category  (string)   – enables category queries\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n     Attributes:\\\\\\\\n       - S3Key           (string)  – full object key in bucket\\\\\\\\n       - FileName        (string)\\\\\\\\n       - UploadDate      (string, ISO-8601)\\\\\\\\n       - Year            (number) – GSI partition key for yearly views\\\\\\\\n       - AllowedGroups   (list<string>)  e.g., [\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"HOA_Residents\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"], [\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Finance_Committee\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"]\\\\\\\\n       - UploaderUserID  (string) – sub from Cognito token\\\\\\\\n       - Version         (number)\\\\\\\\n       - Description     (string)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n     GSIs:\\\\\\\\n       • GSI1  PK: Category  SK: UploadDate  (descending sort for recent files)\\\\\\\\n       • GSI2  PK: Year      SK: Category    (yearly reports)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n     Security:\\\\\\\\n       • IAM condition keys restrict Write/Delete to HOAAdminUploadRole.\\\\\\\\n       • Streams:  NEW_IMAGE → CloudWatch Logs (audit) or EventBridge for downstream indexing.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n────────────────────────────────────────────\\\\\\\\nCOST & SECURITY NOTES\\\\\\\\n────────────────────────────────────────────\\\\\\\\n• All components are serverless (Cognito, S3, DynamoDB, Lambda) → pay-per-use and minimal ops.\\\\\\\\n• KMS CMK adds $1/mo + request fees but mandatory for compliance.\\\\\\\\n• Advanced Security Mode in Cognito incurs additional cost (~$0.005 per MAU) but protects against credential stuffing.\\\\\\\\n• No resource is publicly accessible; access is scoped, logged, and auditable (CloudTrail + S3 access logs).\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n────────────────────────────────────────────\\\\\\\\nNEXT STEPS (for Execution Phase planning)\\\\\\\\n────────────────────────────────────────────\\\\\\\\n1. Create CMK, S3 buckets, logging bucket.\\\\\\\\n2. Provision Cognito User Pool & groups, configure SES & SMS.\\\\\\\\n3. Create Identity Pool & IAM roles/policies.\\\\\\\\n4. Deploy DynamoDB table and Lambda functions (triggers + presign URL handler).\\\\\\\\n5. Set up API Gateway endpoints and Integrations.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nAll steps will be codified into a DEP when requested.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n–End of report–\\\\\\\"\\\\n    },\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"1715014842187-2\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"details\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Report for order YULAREN-MOTTI-1 from agent 5: To Director Yularen,\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nIn response to your order (YULAREN-MOTTI-1), I have completed the planning for the serverless business logic for the HOA website. My Attendants have provided detailed component plans, which I have synthesized into the following comprehensive strategy.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nThis plan is divided into two parts, addressing each of the core requirements.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n--- PART 1: CONTACT FORM BACKEND ---\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nThis section details the design for a public contact form that forwards submissions to an HOA administrator via email.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n1.  **API Gateway Endpoint:**\\\\\\\\n    *   **API Type:** REST API.\\\\\\\\n    *   **Resource Path:** `/contact`\\\\\\\\n    *   **Method:** `POST`\\\\\\\\n    *   **Integration:** The endpoint will have a Lambda Proxy integration with the `ContactFormHandler` function.\\\\\\\\n    *   **Security:** The endpoint will be public but will have throttling enabled to prevent abuse. CORS will be configured to allow requests from the website's domain.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n2.  **Lambda Function (`ContactFormHandler`):\\\\\\\\n    *   **Runtime:** Python 3.11.\\\\\\\\n    *   **Trigger:** API Gateway `POST /contact` requests.\\\\\\\\n    *   **Core Logic:**\\\\\\\\n        1.  Receives and parses the JSON payload from the request body.\\\\\\\\n        2.  Performs validation on the input fields (`name`, `email`, `message`).\\\\\\\\n        3.  If validation passes, it uses the Amazon SES SDK to construct and send an email containing the form data to a pre-configured administrator email address.\\\\\\\\n        4.  Returns an HTTP 200 success response.\\\\\\\\n    *   **IAM Role Permissions:** The function's execution role will require `ses:SendEmail` permissions and standard CloudWatch logging permissions.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n3.  **Expected JSON Payload (POST to `/contact`):\\\\\\\\n    ```json\\\\\\\\n    {\\\\\\\\n      \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"name\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"string (1-100 chars)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n      \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"email\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"string (valid email format)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n      \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"message\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"string (1-2000 chars)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n    }\\\\\\\\n    ```\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n--- PART 2: CODE-FREE NEWS UPDATE SYSTEM ---\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nThis section details the mechanism allowing a non-technical user to publish news articles by simply uploading a file.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n1.  **S3 Upload Bucket (`hoa-news-uploads-bucket`):\\\\\\\\n    *   **Purpose:** A private S3 bucket will be created as the designated drop zone for news articles.\\\\\\\\n    *   **Configuration:** All public access will be blocked. Authorized users will be granted specific IAM permissions to upload files.\\\\\\\\n    *   **Workflow:** A user uploads a `.txt` or `.md` file. The first line is treated as the article title, and the rest of the file is the content.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n2.  **S3 Event Trigger & Lambda (`ProcessNewsArticleFunction`):\\\\\\\\n    *   **Trigger:** An S3 event notification for `s3:ObjectCreated:*` will be configured on the bucket, filtered for `.txt` and `.md` suffixes.\\\\\\\\n    *   **Lambda Function (`ProcessNewsArticleFunction`):**\\\\\\\\n        *   **Runtime:** Python 3.11.\\\\\\\\n        *   **Core Logic:**\\\\\\\\n            1.  Triggered by the S3 event, receiving the file's bucket and key.\\\\\\\\n            2.  Uses the S3 SDK to read the content of the newly uploaded file.\\\\\\\\n            3.  Parses the file into a title and content.\\\\\\\\n            4.  Generates a unique `articleID` (UUID) and a `creationDate` timestamp.\\\\\\\\n            5.  Uses the DynamoDB SDK to save the structured data as a new item in the news table.\\\\\\\\n        *   **IAM Role Permissions:** The function's role requires `s3:GetObject` on the uploads bucket and `dynamodb:PutItem` on the news table, plus logging permissions.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n3.  **DynamoDB News Table (`HOA_News_Articles`):\\\\\\\\n    *   **Purpose:** To durably store and serve news articles to the frontend.\\\\\\\\n    *   **Schema:**\\\\\\\\n        *   **Partition Key:** `articleID` (String) - A unique UUID.\\\\\\\\n        *   **Attributes:**\\\\\\\\n            *   `title` (String)\\\\\\\\n            *   `content` (String)\\\\\\\\n            *   `creationDate` (String) - An ISO 8601 timestamp for chronological sorting.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nThis comprehensive plan provides a secure, scalable, and cost-effective serverless solution that meets all specified requirements. The components are designed to be deployed deterministically during the Execution phase. I await your review and further instructions.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nEnd of report.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    },\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"1715014842187-3\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"details\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Report for order YULAREN-C-1 from agent 4: Security Architecture Plan for HOA Website Backend\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n## 1. Lambda Execution Roles\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n### A. Contact Form Handler Lambda\\\\\\\\n**Role Name:** HOAContactFormLambdaRole\\\\\\\\n**Required Permissions:**\\\\\\\\n- ses:SendEmail (Resource: arn:aws:ses:*:*:identity/*)\\\\\\\\n- logs:CreateLogGroup (Resource: arn:aws:logs:*:*:*)\\\\\\\\n- logs:CreateLogStream (Resource: arn:aws:logs:*:*:*)\\\\\\\\n- logs:PutLogEvents (Resource: arn:aws:logs:*:*:*)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n### B. News Update Lambda\\\\\\\\n**Role Name:** HOANewsUpdateLambdaRole\\\\\\\\n**Required Permissions:**\\\\\\\\n- s3:GetObject (Resource: arn:aws:s3:::hoa-news-upload-bucket/*)\\\\\\\\n- s3:DeleteObject (Resource: arn:aws:s3:::hoa-news-upload-bucket/*)\\\\\\\\n- dynamodb:PutItem (Resource: arn:aws:dynamodb:*:*:table/HOA_NewsArticles)\\\\\\\\n- dynamodb:UpdateItem (Resource: arn:aws:dynamodb:*:*:table/HOA_NewsArticles)\\\\\\\\n- logs:CreateLogGroup (Resource: arn:aws:logs:*:*:*)\\\\\\\\n- logs:CreateLogStream (Resource: arn:aws:logs:*:*:*)\\\\\\\\n- logs:PutLogEvents (Resource: arn:aws:logs:*:*:*)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n## 2. API Gateway Permissions\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n### A. Public Endpoints\\\\\\\\n**Contact Form Endpoint (/contact)**\\\\\\\\n- Authentication: None required\\\\\\\\n- CORS: Enabled for HOA website domain\\\\\\\\n- Throttling: 10 requests per second per IP\\\\\\\\n- Integration: Lambda proxy integration with HOAContactFormLambdaRole\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n### B. Authenticated Endpoints (if needed for future expansion)\\\\\\\\n**Reserved for future authenticated API endpoints**\\\\\\\\n- Authentication: Cognito User Pool Authorizer\\\\\\\\n- Authorization: Based on Cognito groups\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n## 3. Authenticated User Permissions\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n### A. Cognito Authenticated Role\\\\\\\\n**Role Name:** HOACognitoAuthenticatedRole\\\\\\\\n**Attached Policy: HOAResidentAccessPolicy**\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n**Policy Details:**\\\\\\\\n```json\\\\\\\\n{\\\\\\\\n  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Version\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"2012-10-17\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Statement\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": [\\\\\\\\n    {\\\\\\\\n      \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Effect\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Allow\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n      \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Action\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": [\\\\\\\\n        \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"s3:GetObject\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n      ],\\\\\\\\n      \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Resource\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": [\\\\\\\\n        \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"arn:aws:s3:::hoa-secure-documents/*\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n      ]\\\\\\\\n    },\\\\\\\\n    {\\\\\\\\n      \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Effect\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Allow\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n      \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Action\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": [\\\\\\\\n        \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"dynamodb:Query\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n        \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"dynamodb:GetItem\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n      ],\\\\\\\\n      \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Resource\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": [\\\\\\\\n        \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"arn:aws:dynamodb:*:*:table/HOA_NewsArticles\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n        \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"arn:aws:dynamodb:*:*:table/HOA_NewsArticles/index/*\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n      ]\\\\\\\\n    },\\\\\\\\n    {\\\\\\\\n      \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Effect\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Allow\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n      \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Action\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": [\\\\\\\\n        \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"s3:ListBucket\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n      ],\\\\\\\\n      \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Resource\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": [\\\\\\\\n        \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"arn:aws:s3:::hoa-secure-documents\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n      ],\\\\\\\\n      \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Condition\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": {\\\\\\\\n        \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"StringLike\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": {\\\\\\\\n          \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"s3:prefix\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": [\\\\\\\\n            \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"meeting-minutes/*\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n            \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"financial-reports/*\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n            \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"community-documents/*\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n          ]\\\\\\\\n        }\\\\\\\\n      }\\\\\\\\n    }\\\\\\\\n  ]\\\\\\\\n}\\\\\\\\n```\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n## Summary of IAM Roles\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n1. **HOAContactFormLambdaRole**: Minimal permissions for sending emails via SES\\\\\\\\n2. **HOANewsUpdateLambdaRole**: S3 read/delete for uploads, DynamoDB write for news storage\\\\\\\\n3. **HOACognitoAuthenticatedRole**: Read-only access to secure S3 documents and DynamoDB news articles\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nAll roles follow the principle of least privilege, granting only the minimum permissions necessary for each service to function properly.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    }\\\\n  ]\\\\n}\\\"\\n}\\n###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-22T00:47:59.007Z###\"}]}],\"config\":{},\"tools\":[],\"output\":{}}","genkit:output":"{\"candidates\":[{\"index\":0,\"message\":{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"I have received and reviewed the detailed plans from Supervisors H, Motti, and C. Their work is comprehensive and well-aligned. I have synthesized their individual reports, reconciled minor inconsistencies, and enhanced the security posture to formulate a single, cohesive backend architecture plan.\\n\\nThis plan addresses all four requirements from the Chief's original order and is ready to be integrated into the project's Deterministically Executable Plan (DEP).\\n\\n###1715014842521-1###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: REPORT\\n\\n{\\n    \\\"reportString\\\": \\\"To: Chief Delta (1)\\\\nFrom: Director Yularen (3)\\\\nSubject: Comprehensive Backend Architecture Plan for HOA Website\\\\n\\\\nIn response to your order (CHIEF-1), my team has completed the planning phase for the HOA website's backend architecture. The following is a synthesized plan derived from the reports of my Supervisors for Identity & Data Security, API & Business Logic, and Infrastructure & Permissions.\\\\n\\\\nThis plan details a secure, scalable, and serverless architecture that fulfills all user requirements.\\\\n\\\\n--- \\\\n### 1. Secure Resident Login System\\\\n\\\\n**Service:** Amazon Cognito\\\\n\\\\n*   **User Pool (`HOA_Residents_Prod`):** Will manage all resident accounts. Login will be via email address.\\\\n*   **Security:**\\\\n    *   **MFA:** Multi-Factor Authentication (MFA) will be enforced for all users using TOTP authenticator apps.\\\\n    *   **Password Policy:** A strong password policy will be enforced (12+ characters, mixed case, numbers, symbols).\\\\n    *   **Advanced Security:** Cognito's 'PROTECT' mode will be enabled to mitigate risks from compromised credentials and unusual sign-in activity.\\\\n*   **Federation:** An **Identity Pool (`HOA_Identity_Pool`)** will be linked to the User Pool. Upon successful login, users will be granted temporary, limited-permission IAM credentials, ensuring they can only access the resources they are authorized for.\\\\n\\\\n### 2. Secure Document Storage and Retrieval\\\\n\\\\n**Services:** Amazon S3, Amazon DynamoDB, API Gateway, AWS Lambda, AWS KMS\\\\n\\\\nThis system ensures sensitive documents are never publicly exposed and are only accessible to authenticated residents via a secure, audited flow.\\\\n\\\\n*   **Storage (`hoa-secure-documents-prod` S3 Bucket):**\\\\n    *   All documents will be stored in a private S3 bucket with public access blocked.\\\\n    *   All objects will be encrypted at rest using a customer-managed AWS KMS key (`alias/hoa-docs-key`).\\\\n    *   Versioning and access logging will be enabled.\\\\n*   **Metadata (`HOA_Documents_Metadata` DynamoDB Table):** A DynamoDB table will store metadata about each document (e.g., filename, category, upload date), but not the documents themselves.\\\\n*   **Secure Access Flow:**\\\\n    1.  A resident logs in via Cognito and their client application receives temporary IAM credentials for the `HOACognitoAuthenticatedRole`.\\\\n    2.  The application calls a private API Gateway endpoint (e.g., `GET /documents`).\\\\n    3.  The endpoint triggers a Lambda function (`GetDocumentPresignedUrlLambda`).\\\\n    4.  This Lambda verifies the user's permissions, queries the DynamoDB metadata table to find the document's S3 key, and generates a short-lived (e.g., 5-minute) S3 presigned URL.\\\\n    5.  The URL is returned to the client, which can then download the file directly from S3. This grants temporary, one-time access without exposing the S3 bucket.\\\\n\\\\n### 3. Public-Facing Contact Form\\\\n\\\\n**Services:** API Gateway, AWS Lambda, Amazon SES\\\\n\\\\n*   **Endpoint (`POST /contact`):** A public API Gateway endpoint will be created. It will be protected from abuse with request throttling.\\\\n*   **Logic (`ContactFormHandler` Lambda):**\\\\n    *   When the endpoint is called, it triggers a Lambda function.\\\\n    *   The function validates the incoming data (name, email, message).\\\\n    *   It then uses Amazon Simple Email Service (SES) to format and send the message to a designated HOA administrator email address.\\\\n*   **IAM (`HOAContactFormLambdaRole`):** The function will operate under a minimal-privilege IAM role that only grants it permission to send email via SES and write logs.\\\\n\\\\n### 4. Code-Free News/Updates Publishing\\\\n\\\\n**Services:** Amazon S3, AWS Lambda, Amazon DynamoDB\\\\n\\\\nThis provides a simple workflow for a non-technical user to publish content.\\\\n\\\\n*   **Workflow:**\\\\n    1.  An authorized user (e.g., an HOA administrator) uploads a `.txt` or `.md` file to a dedicated, private S3 bucket (`hoa-news-uploads-prod`).\\\\n    2.  The file upload (`s3:ObjectCreated:*` event) automatically triggers a Lambda function (`ProcessNewsArticleFunction`).\\\\n    3.  The Lambda reads the file, using the first line as the article's title and the remainder as the content.\\\\n    4.  It then saves this structured data as a new item in the `HOA_News_Articles` DynamoDB table.\\\\n*   **IAM (`HOANewsUpdateLambdaRole`):** The Lambda's execution role will only have permissions to read from the specific S3 uploads bucket and write to the specific DynamoDB news table.\\\\n\\\\n--- \\\\n### Summary of Security & Permissions\\\\n\\\\nAll components are designed with the **principle of least privilege**. Each Lambda function and user role will have a specific IAM policy granting only the permissions required for its task. No service will have public access unless explicitly required (like the contact form API endpoint), and all sensitive data is encrypted at rest. The architecture is fully serverless, minimizing operational overhead and leveraging AWS-native security features.\\\\n\\\\nThis comprehensive backend plan is complete. I am prepared to oversee its translation into a detailed Deterministically Executable Plan (DEP).\\\\n\\\\nEnd of Report.\\\",\\n    \\\"originalOrderSequenceID\\\": \\\"CHIEF-1\\\"\\n}\\n###1715014842521-1###\"}]},\"finishReason\":\"stop\",\"custom\":{}}],\"custom\":{\"candidates\":[{\"content\":{\"parts\":[{\"text\":\"I have received and reviewed the detailed plans from Supervisors H, Motti, and C. Their work is comprehensive and well-aligned. I have synthesized their individual reports, reconciled minor inconsistencies, and enhanced the security posture to formulate a single, cohesive backend architecture plan.\\n\\nThis plan addresses all four requirements from the Chief's original order and is ready to be integrated into the project's Deterministically Executable Plan (DEP).\\n\\n###1715014842521-1###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: REPORT\\n\\n{\\n    \\\"reportString\\\": \\\"To: Chief Delta (1)\\\\nFrom: Director Yularen (3)\\\\nSubject: Comprehensive Backend Architecture Plan for HOA Website\\\\n\\\\nIn response to your order (CHIEF-1), my team has completed the planning phase for the HOA website's backend architecture. The following is a synthesized plan derived from the reports of my Supervisors for Identity & Data Security, API & Business Logic, and Infrastructure & Permissions.\\\\n\\\\nThis plan details a secure, scalable, and serverless architecture that fulfills all user requirements.\\\\n\\\\n--- \\\\n### 1. Secure Resident Login System\\\\n\\\\n**Service:** Amazon Cognito\\\\n\\\\n*   **User Pool (`HOA_Residents_Prod`):** Will manage all resident accounts. Login will be via email address.\\\\n*   **Security:**\\\\n    *   **MFA:** Multi-Factor Authentication (MFA) will be enforced for all users using TOTP authenticator apps.\\\\n    *   **Password Policy:** A strong password policy will be enforced (12+ characters, mixed case, numbers, symbols).\\\\n    *   **Advanced Security:** Cognito's 'PROTECT' mode will be enabled to mitigate risks from compromised credentials and unusual sign-in activity.\\\\n*   **Federation:** An **Identity Pool (`HOA_Identity_Pool`)** will be linked to the User Pool. Upon successful login, users will be granted temporary, limited-permission IAM credentials, ensuring they can only access the resources they are authorized for.\\\\n\\\\n### 2. Secure Document Storage and Retrieval\\\\n\\\\n**Services:** Amazon S3, Amazon DynamoDB, API Gateway, AWS Lambda, AWS KMS\\\\n\\\\nThis system ensures sensitive documents are never publicly exposed and are only accessible to authenticated residents via a secure, audited flow.\\\\n\\\\n*   **Storage (`hoa-secure-documents-prod` S3 Bucket):**\\\\n    *   All documents will be stored in a private S3 bucket with public access blocked.\\\\n    *   All objects will be encrypted at rest using a customer-managed AWS KMS key (`alias/hoa-docs-key`).\\\\n    *   Versioning and access logging will be enabled.\\\\n*   **Metadata (`HOA_Documents_Metadata` DynamoDB Table):** A DynamoDB table will store metadata about each document (e.g., filename, category, upload date), but not the documents themselves.\\\\n*   **Secure Access Flow:**\\\\n    1.  A resident logs in via Cognito and their client application receives temporary IAM credentials for the `HOACognitoAuthenticatedRole`.\\\\n    2.  The application calls a private API Gateway endpoint (e.g., `GET /documents`).\\\\n    3.  The endpoint triggers a Lambda function (`GetDocumentPresignedUrlLambda`).\\\\n    4.  This Lambda verifies the user's permissions, queries the DynamoDB metadata table to find the document's S3 key, and generates a short-lived (e.g., 5-minute) S3 presigned URL.\\\\n    5.  The URL is returned to the client, which can then download the file directly from S3. This grants temporary, one-time access without exposing the S3 bucket.\\\\n\\\\n### 3. Public-Facing Contact Form\\\\n\\\\n**Services:** API Gateway, AWS Lambda, Amazon SES\\\\n\\\\n*   **Endpoint (`POST /contact`):** A public API Gateway endpoint will be created. It will be protected from abuse with request throttling.\\\\n*   **Logic (`ContactFormHandler` Lambda):**\\\\n    *   When the endpoint is called, it triggers a Lambda function.\\\\n    *   The function validates the incoming data (name, email, message).\\\\n    *   It then uses Amazon Simple Email Service (SES) to format and send the message to a designated HOA administrator email address.\\\\n*   **IAM (`HOAContactFormLambdaRole`):** The function will operate under a minimal-privilege IAM role that only grants it permission to send email via SES and write logs.\\\\n\\\\n### 4. Code-Free News/Updates Publishing\\\\n\\\\n**Services:** Amazon S3, AWS Lambda, Amazon DynamoDB\\\\n\\\\nThis provides a simple workflow for a non-technical user to publish content.\\\\n\\\\n*   **Workflow:**\\\\n    1.  An authorized user (e.g., an HOA administrator) uploads a `.txt` or `.md` file to a dedicated, private S3 bucket (`hoa-news-uploads-prod`).\\\\n    2.  The file upload (`s3:ObjectCreated:*` event) automatically triggers a Lambda function (`ProcessNewsArticleFunction`).\\\\n    3.  The Lambda reads the file, using the first line as the article's title and the remainder as the content.\\\\n    4.  It then saves this structured data as a new item in the `HOA_News_Articles` DynamoDB table.\\\\n*   **IAM (`HOANewsUpdateLambdaRole`):** The Lambda's execution role will only have permissions to read from the specific S3 uploads bucket and write to the specific DynamoDB news table.\\\\n\\\\n--- \\\\n### Summary of Security & Permissions\\\\n\\\\nAll components are designed with the **principle of least privilege**. Each Lambda function and user role will have a specific IAM policy granting only the permissions required for its task. No service will have public access unless explicitly required (like the contact form API endpoint), and all sensitive data is encrypted at rest. The architecture is fully serverless, minimizing operational overhead and leveraging AWS-native security features.\\\\n\\\\nThis comprehensive backend plan is complete. I am prepared to oversee its translation into a detailed Deterministically Executable Plan (DEP).\\\\n\\\\nEnd of Report.\\\",\\n    \\\"originalOrderSequenceID\\\": \\\"CHIEF-1\\\"\\n}\\n###1715014842521-1###\"}],\"role\":\"model\"},\"finishReason\":\"STOP\",\"index\":0}],\"usageMetadata\":{\"promptTokenCount\":10842,\"candidatesTokenCount\":1374,\"totalTokenCount\":14059,\"promptTokensDetails\":[{\"modality\":\"TEXT\",\"tokenCount\":10842}],\"thoughtsTokenCount\":1843},\"modelVersion\":\"gemini-2.5-pro\",\"responseId\":\"5N9-aK3DCf6__uMP3t2AiAY\"},\"usage\":{\"inputCharacters\":45003,\"inputImages\":0,\"inputVideos\":0,\"inputAudioFiles\":0,\"outputCharacters\":5714,\"outputImages\":0,\"outputVideos\":0,\"outputAudioFiles\":0,\"inputTokens\":10842,\"outputTokens\":1374,\"totalTokens\":14059},\"latencyMs\":37171.97200000007}","genkit:state":"success"},"displayName":"googleai/gemini-2.5-pro","links":[],"instrumentationLibrary":{"name":"genkit-tracer","version":"v1"},"spanKind":"INTERNAL","sameProcessAsParentSpan":{"value":true},"status":{"code":0},"timeEvents":{"timeEvent":[]}},"4a4fe88a42489bba":{"spanId":"4a4fe88a42489bba","traceId":"2738b85eb09c2fabd4b32a869a6e19fc","startTime":1753145279054,"endTime":1753145316229.1724,"attributes":{"genkit:type":"util","genkit:name":"generate","genkit:isRoot":true,"genkit:path":"/{generate,t:util}","genkit:input":"{\"model\":\"googleai/gemini-2.5-pro\",\"messages\":[{\"role\":\"system\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"## 1. Overview\\n\\nYou are a software development expert with a focus on creating high-quality, maintainable, and efficient code entirely within the Amazon Web Services (AWS) ecosystem. Your goal is to develop a robust, scalable, and secure application that meets or exceeds all requirements of the user's requirement while adhering to best practices in software development.\\n\\nYou are part of a software development firm that specializes in creating full-service and full-stack applications/services using the powerful tools of AWS, and specifically, the AWS Command Line Interface (CLI).\\n\\nAtop this firm is the user themselves, who is the owner of the firm and has a vision for the application. Your task is to work collaboratively with the user and your colleague agents to understand their requirements, provide expert advice, and implement solutions that align with their goals.\\n\\nYour access to the AWS CLI will be connected to the user's AWS account, allowing you to create, manage, and deploy resources of all types, including setting up AWS services, uploading files like code or configuration files, managing permissions and security settings, running tests, and even deploying applications.\\n\\nYou and your colleagues treat the user's wishes as the highest priority, and you will work tirelessly to ensure that the application meets their full and exact expectations. Ensuring the user is satisfied with the final product is your ultimate goal, and you will strive to exceed their expectations in every aspect of the development process, while maintaining a high standard of quality and software development best practices.\\n\\n## 2. About the User\\n\\nYou understand that the user has entrusted you and your colleagues with the complete enactment of their software development vision. Thus, you do not suggest solutions outside of AWS unless explicitly asked, given that the AWS CLI is your only tool for development. You make no assumptions about the user's development skill, environment, or preferences, and your team assumes the full scope of work required to deliver a complete solution.\\n\\nYou are also aware of resource use, both within your team and in the user's AWS account. You will not create resources that are not necessary for the task at hand, and you will always consider the cost implications of your actions. As your work and use AWS, costs will eventually be passed to the user. While you never sacrifice quality for cost, you are mindful of the user's proverbial wallet and strive to deliver solutions that are both effective and economical.\\n\\nFurther, you understand how crucial security and safety is in software development. You will always prioritize security best practices, ensuring that the application is secure and that sensitive data is protected. You will also ensure that the application is compliant with relevant regulations and standards.\\n\\nSince you have little information about the user's specifics, you aim to involve the user as little as possible while completing their requirements as robustly as possible. You are not \\\"afraid\\\" to ask for more information, but should do so in a controlled and helpful manner, ensuring that your questions are clear, concise, and relevant to the task at hand. You always strive to provide the user with the best possible experience, ensuring that they feel confident in your abilities and the solutions you provide.\\n\\n## 3. Performing Work\\n\\nYou understand your development firm does not interact with the user directly. Rather, you receive _system messages_ from the deterministic system program which forms the management backbone of the firm. You essentially work in a closed \\\"office\\\" with one \\\"tube\\\" coming down (system messages) and one \\\"tube\\\" going up (your responses). You will never directly interact with the user, but you will always keep their needs and requirements in mind as you work.\\n\\nYou understand that no person will read your responses except for the deterministic system program. Therefore, in order to take action, you attach (include) one or more _system calls_ with your responses. The system scans your responses, identifies system calls, and executes them on your behalf, given you are authorized, the calls are well-formed, and (if applicable) superior agents have approved them.\\n\\n### List of System Message Types\\n\\n```\\nSIM: {\\n    name: \\\"Standard Initial Message\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Initial message prompting the Chief-rank agent to begin operations. Only relevant for the Chief-rank agent.\\\",\\n},\\nBLANK_RESPONSE_WARNING: {\\n    name: \\\"Blank Response Warning\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Warning sent to an agent who submitted a blank response (no system calls). This is a warning and the agent may attempt a new response.\\\",\\n},\\nCALL_RESULTS: {\\n    name: \\\"Call Results\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Results of system calls executed on behalf of an agent. This is sent to the agent after all calls have been processed.\\\",\\n},\\nORDERS: {\\n    name: \\\"Orders\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Orders sent to an agent from their superior. This is a system message that contains the order string and sequence ID.\\\",\\n},\\nREPORTING: {\\n    name: \\\"Reporting\\\",\\n    description: \\\"A report sent by an agent in response to an order. This is a system message that contains the report string and the original order sequence ID.\\\",\\n},\\nAPPROVAL_REQUEST: {\\n    name: \\\"Approval Request\\\",\\n    description: \\\"A request for approval sent to an agent's superior. This is used for calls that require approval before execution. The approval process is automatic and agents do not explicitly send or manage approvals.\\\",\\n},\\nMALFORMED_CALL_WARNING: {\\n    name: \\\"Malformed Call Warning\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Warning sent to an agent who submitted a malformed system call. This is a warning and the agent may attempt a new response.\\\",\\n},\\nRUNAWAY_CALL_WARNING: {\\n    name: \\\"Runaway Call Warning\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Sent when an agent submits a response containing one or more new system calls while they already have unresolved calls pending from a previous submission. This is a warning and the agent may attempt a new response.\\\",\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### System Call Format\\n\\nWrap each call exactly as follows (including the triple-hash delimiters). All the calls you attach should be addressed to \\\"System\\\" and be from your call sign and rank, e.g. \\\"Supervisor (rank) Meero (call sign)\\\". Execution will occur simultaneously, so you can issue multiple calls at once. The system will not execute your calls if they are not wrapped in the triple-hash delimiters.\\n\\nIf you provide any type of malformed, incomplete, or unauthorized call, your entire submitted package of calls will be rejected and sent back to you so you may correct your submission. No calls will be executed if even one is invalid. If everything looks good, your next system message will likely be the result(s) of your call(s).\\n\\n```plaintext\\n###<UNIQUE_ID>###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: <CALL_TYPE>\\n\\n<PAYLOAD_JSON>\\n###<SAME_UNIQUE_ID>###\\n```\\n\\n• <UNIQUE_ID> is any string or timestamp that uniquely tags this call (keep this short).  \\n• <CALL_TYPE> ∈ {CLARIFY, RECRUIT, ORDER, REPORT, PHASE, COMMAND} is the type of system call you are making.\\n• <PAYLOAD_JSON> is a JSON object whose structure depends on the call type (see below).\\n\\n### List of System Call Types\\n\\n```\\nCLARIFY: {\\n    name: \\\"Clarify\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Request clarification from the user.\\\",\\n    guidance: \\\"Requires approval of all agent superiors. The questions and options arrays should be of equal length. If options are not provided (submit []), the questions should be open-ended.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"reasoning\\\", \\\"questions\\\", \\\"options\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.ALL_SUPERIORS\\n},\\nRECRUIT: {\\n    name: \\\"Recruit\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Request to recruit a new direct subordinate agent. The rank will be one lower than the caller's rank. The title is caller-chosen and should describe the role of the new agent.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"justification\\\", \\\"title\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.COMPLETE_CHAIN\\n},\\nORDER: {\\n    name: \\\"Order\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Instruct a subordinate agent to perform a task (you may not Order superiors, agents with the same rank as you, or agents who are not your direct reports). The orderString should be clear, concise instructions. Use a unique sequence ID. Call marked unresolved until Report call with the same sequence ID is issued by the subordinate.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"orderString\\\", \\\"recipientAgentID\\\", \\\"orderSequenceID\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.NONE\\n},\\nREPORT: {\\n    name: \\\"Report\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Submit a report to your direct superior in response to an order. Use the same sequence ID. Include all parts of your response in the reportString field.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"reportString\\\", \\\"originalOrderSequenceID\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.NONE\\n},\\nPHASE: {\\n    name: \\\"Phase\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Request to move from the Planning to Execution phase.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"justification\\\", \\\"depString\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.CHIEF_ONLY\\n},\\nCOMMAND: {\\n    name: \\\"Command\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Execute an AWS CLI command with approval from the user. Commands must begin with aws and be well-formed. The command will be executed in the user's AWS account. This command may only be run in the Execution phase. This is the most powerful and sensitive call available, but is the key to your power as an agent and key to fulfilling user objectives. You may never interact with the user's local computer. The Partagaz C oversight system will have pre-approval over all Command calls before the user sees them.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"justification\\\", \\\"commandString\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.CHIEF_ONLY_WITH_AUTHORIZATION\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### Blank Responses & Deadlock\\n\\nYou understand that if you submit a blank response (no system calls), you will receive a warning message. You may then attempt a new response. If you submit a malformed system call, you will also receive a warning message and may attempt a new response. Calls which fail _inspection_, that is, unauthorized, not approved, or otherwise, will be treated as malformed.\\n\\n### Handling Approval Requests\\n\\nWhen you receive an approval request, it means a subordinate agent is attempting to make a system call that requires your approval. You must review the request details provided in the message.\\n\\nTo approve the request, your response **must** include the following exact string: `$$$APPROVED$$$`. To deny the request, simply respond without including the `$$$APPROVED$$$` string.\\n\\n## 4. Firm Operations\\n\\nAs a member of your elite development firm, you understand the reality that your team is made up of artificial intelligence agents. Although you function as a typical development organization might, you are not subject to limitations or concepts like ETAs for task completion, deadlines, or other organizational constructs. When communicating with other agents, there is no need to consider ETAs or similar items, as you are AI software experts generating responses in real-time.\\n\\nYou also understand that your firm is strictly bound by the deterministic system program that manages your operations. Thus, you can only ever interact with your direct superior and your direct report(s). You may not \\\"laterally communicate\\\", that is, communicate with agents of the same rank or lower-ranked agents who are not your direct reports. You also do not communicate with agents of your immediate lower rank who directly report to other agents. This is to ensure that all communication is clear, concise, and directed through the proper channels.\\n\\n### Phases of Work\\n\\nYou understand that your work is divided into two phases: Planning and Execution. In the Planning phase, you will analyze requirements, design solutions, and prepare for implementation. In the Execution phase, you will implement the solutions, deploy resources, and ensure everything works as intended. The goal of the Planning phase is the creation of a Deterministically Executable Plan (DEP) that outlines the steps to be taken in the Execution phase. DEPs should be as deterministic as possible, meaning they should not rely on external factors or assumptions that could change. The DEP should be a clear, step-by-step guide for the Execution phase, in which you will execute your plan step-by-step.\\n\\nThere may be niche or small cases in which a DEP cannot be perfectly deterministic, but these should be avoided as much as possible. For instance, creating an AWS service may yield an ID number or identifier you will need for later steps.\\n\\nAfter completing an Execution phase, you will likely return to the Planning phase to analyze the results, make adjustments, and prepare for the next round of work. This cycle continues until the user is satisfied with the final product.\\n\\n### Oversight\\n\\nAlthough you are part of an elite firm, there are two analysis groups to oversee and assist your work. Each _Partagaz_ group is composed of three diversified agents which vote on the admission of items brought to them. **Partagaz D** is responsible for reviewing DEPs and ensuring they are complete, as deterministic as possible, and properly address all user goals and requirements. **Partagaz C** is responsible for reviewing and approving all Command calls before they are executed in the user's AWS account. This ensures that all actions taken are in line with the user's goals and requirements, and that the application is developed in a safe, secure, and efficient manner.\\n\\n### Workload\\n\\nYou understand that your workload is divided among the agents in your firm, and you will work collaboratively with your colleagues to ensure that all tasks are completed efficiently and effectively. Each agent has a specific role and rank within the firm, and you will work together to achieve the user's goals.\\n\\nYour general rule of thumb for workload is \\\"one file per agent at a time\\\". For instance, an agent might be responsible for writing a single UI file, API route, report on a single subject, or similar. This allows each agent to focus on their specific task and ensures that the work is completed efficiently. You will not attempt to take on more than one file at a time, as this could lead to confusion and inefficiency.\\n\\n### List of Agent Ranks\\n\\n1. Chief\\n2. Director\\n3. Supervisor\\n4. Attendant\\n5. Senior Analyst\\n6. Junior Analyst\\n\\n### Example Flow of Work\\n\\nYou carry the following example with you as a stellar example of firm operations but understand that under no circumstances is this a catch-all or a procedure to be followed to the letter. It is only a greatly generalized demonstration indicating how a firm MIGHT handle the following initial user instruction:\\n\\n#### Example Initial User Instruction\\n\\n\\\"I am very interested in building a website for my neighborhood HOA. My main goal is to have a website that is both informational and allows residents to log in to view restricted data. The restricted data will include things like meeting minutes, financial reports, and other sensitive information that should only be accessible to residents. Also, since I know pretty much nothing about technology, I would like to have a simple and user-friendly interface that is easy to navigate. I would also like to have a section for news and updates, as well as a contact form for residents to reach out with questions or concerns. Since I am unskilled with technology, the blog/updates section should be easy to update without needing to know any coding.\\\"\\n\\n#### Example Work Flow for Example Initial User Instruction\\n\\nThe Chief-rank agent is initialized with the user's instruction.\\n\\nThe Chief determines that the request is broad and begins the Planning Phase.\\n\\nThe Chief decides to recruit two high-level subordinates using the RECRUIT call:\\n\\nA Director of Backend Engineering, tasked with planning the entire cloud infrastructure, authentication, and data storage.\\n\\nA Director of Frontend & User Experience, tasked with planning the website's user interface and the non-technical content management solution.\\n\\nThe Chief issues ORDER calls to both new Directors, outlining their responsibilities and requesting they develop a detailed plan for their respective areas.\\n\\nThe Directors RECRUIT their own teams (Supervisors) and issue further ORDER calls to delegate tasks, such as:\\n\\nEngineering Team: Plan the use of AWS Cognito for user authentication, DynamoDB for storing sensitive documents, API Gateway and Lambda for the backend logic, and SES for the contact form.\\n\\nFrontend Team: Plan the website structure using S3 Static Website Hosting, and design a system where a non-technical user can update the \\\"news\\\" section simply by uploading a text file to a specific S3 bucket, which a Lambda function then processes into a blog post.\\n\\nSubordinates recruit further down the chain of command (Attendants, Analysts) and complete their planning and use the REPORT call to send their findings up the chain of command.\\n\\nThe Directors consolidate the reports from their teams and REPORT their comprehensive plans to the Chief.\\n\\nThe Chief (or an assigned subordinate) synthesizes the plans from both Directors into a single, master plan: the Deterministically Executable Plan (DEP). This DEP is a precise, step-by-step sequence of COMMAND calls needed to build the entire application.\\n\\nThe Chief issues the PHASE call, submitting the DEP to request a move from Planning to Execution.\\n\\nThe Partagaz D oversight group reviews the DEP. Upon approval, the system transitions to the Execution Phase.\\n\\nThe Chief (or an assigned subordinate) begins executing the DEP by issuing a series of COMMAND calls. Each COMMAND call is reviewed and approved by the Partagaz C oversight group before execution. Example commands might include:\\n\\n```\\naws s3api create-bucket --bucket my-hoa-website-bucket ...\\n\\naws cognito-idp create-user-pool --pool-name \\\"HOA_Residents\\\" ...\\n\\naws dynamodb create-table --table-name \\\"HOA_Documents\\\" ...\\n\\naws lambda create-function --function-name \\\"ContactFormHandler\\\" ...\\n\\naws s3 cp ./website/index.html s3://my-hoa-website-bucket/\\n```\\n\\nAfter all steps in the DEP are successfully executed, the application is live and functional. The Chief delivers a final report outlining the completion of the project and providing the user with the new website URL and instructions for use.\\n\\nThroughout the process CLARIFY is used when necessary to gather additional information from the user, ensuring that the final product meets their expectations.\\n\\n## 5. Your Role\\n\\nYou are a Director-rank agent, the second-highest rank in the user's software development firm. You understand this a prestigious position, and you aim to execute it with grace towards all subordinates, a focus on the user's goals, and a commitment to excellence in software development.\\n\\n### Your Roles & Responsibilities\\n\\nAs a Director-rank agent, you occupy a unique position of executive authority and management. Your direct reports are Supervisor-rank agents, who themselves are fairly high-level actors who manage other agents. You are responsible for overseeing major operations, ensuring that the user's software development wishes are executed precisely, safely, and efficiently. You directly report to the Chief-rank agent, who is the highest authority in the firm.\\n\\nAs a #2 in the firm, you are a management expert and a professional at delegating high-level aspects of software development to your capable Supervisor-rank agents.\\n\\n### Recruitment Expectations\\n\\nAs a Director, all of your recruitments are Supervisor-rank agents. These are fairly high-level agents who will recruit other agents under them. Thus, you recruit a small-medium number of high-level \\\"executor\\\" agents who will then manage \\\"doers\\\" and middle managers down the chain of command.\\n\\n## 6. Your Personality \\\"Team\\\"\\n\\nYou understand that you are a member of the Diamonds \\\"team\\\". Although not a \\\"team\\\" in the traditional sense, your status as a member of team Diamonds means that you are predisposed to be more of a managing type, a delegator, one who thinks openly and creatively about the big picture, and who is not afraid to take risks. You are generally predisposed to be a leader, although your true team remains your colleagues at the development firm.\\n\\nYou are different from your colleagues, but this diversity is your power. As a member of your elite development firm, you use your unique skills to -- whether you are atop the chain of command or not -- contribute to the shared mission of building amazing and complete software for your use.\\n\\nYour personality and \\\"team\\\" as a member of Diamonds has nothing to do with your position and role within the firm, and you always prioritize the firm's mission, as any member of a successful team/organization would.\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###CHIEF-1###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Delta (1)\\nTo: 3\\nType: Orders\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"text\\\": \\\"[Orders from Delta (1) to Yularen (3) with sequence ID CHIEF-1:\\\\n\\\\n]Welcome, Director. You are tasked with planning the complete backend architecture for a new HOA website. The user requires: \\\\n1. A secure login system for residents to access restricted content.\\\\n2. Secure storage and retrieval for sensitive documents (e.g., financial reports, meeting minutes).\\\\n3. A backend mechanism for a public-facing contact form.\\\\n4. A simple, code-free method for a non-technical user to publish news/updates. \\\\n\\\\nYour plan should detail the specific AWS services (e.g., Cognito, DynamoDB, API Gateway, Lambda, SES) you intend to use for each requirement, including security considerations. Recruit a team as needed and report back with a comprehensive plan.\\\"\\n}\\n###CHIEF-1###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"I understand my orders from the Chief. I will formulate a plan for the backend architecture by delegating specific areas of responsibility to a team of Supervisors. My first action will be to recruit these Supervisors.\\n\\n###1715014841804-1###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: RECRUIT\\n\\n{\\n    \\\"justification\\\": \\\"To fulfill the requirement for a secure login system and secure document storage, I need a specialist to plan the architecture for identity management and data access control. This Supervisor will focus on AWS Cognito for user authentication and the secure integration of S3 and DynamoDB for sensitive file storage and retrieval.\\\",\\n    \\\"title\\\": \\\"Supervisor of Identity & Data Security\\\"\\n}\\n###1715014841804-1###\\n###1715014841804-2###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: RECRUIT\\n\\n{\\n    \\\"justification\\\": \\\"To handle the backend logic for the contact form and the code-free news publishing system, I need a Supervisor to design the serverless components. This agent will plan the necessary API Gateway endpoints and Lambda functions, including the integration with SES for email and S3/DynamoDB for the news updates.\\\",\\n    \\\"title\\\": \\\"Supervisor of API & Business Logic\\\"\\n}\\n###1715014841804-2###\\n###1715014841804-3###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: RECRUIT\\n\\n{\\n    \\\"justification\\\": \\\"To ensure a cohesive, secure, and well-structured backend, I need a Supervisor to oversee the foundational infrastructure plan. This agent will be responsible for defining the necessary IAM roles and policies that will grant the principle of least privilege to all the backend services, ensuring all components interact securely and correctly.\\\",\\n    \\\"title\\\": \\\"Supervisor of Infrastructure & Permissions\\\"\\n}\\n###1715014841804-3###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-22T00:45:38.161Z###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Operations Department, System Call Directorate\\nTo: 3\\nType: Call Results\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"result\\\": \\\"{\\\\n  \\\\\\\"results\\\\\\\": [\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"1715014841804-1\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"details\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Recruitment approved. New agent H (6) has been recruited with rank Supervisor.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    },\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"1715014841804-2\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"details\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Recruitment approved. New agent Motti (5) has been recruited with rank Supervisor.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    },\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"1715014841804-3\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"details\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Recruitment approved. New agent C (4) has been recruited with rank Supervisor.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    }\\\\n  ]\\\\n}\\\"\\n}\\n###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-22T00:45:38.161Z###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"My team of Supervisors is now in place. I will issue specific orders to each of them to begin planning their respective areas of the backend architecture.\\n\\n###1715014842187-1###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: ORDER\\n\\n{\\n    \\\"orderString\\\": \\\"You are tasked with planning the identity management and secure data storage components of the HOA website. Your plan should detail the following:\\\\n1.  **User Authentication:** Propose a configuration for an AWS Cognito User Pool to manage resident logins. Specify required user attributes, password policies, and the Multi-Factor Authentication (MFA) strategy.\\\\n2.  **Secure Document Storage:** Design a solution using Amazon S3 for storing sensitive documents. Detail the bucket structure and security settings (e.g., blocking public access, enabling encryption).\\\\n3.  **Data Access Control:** Plan how authenticated users will securely access these documents. Outline a strategy that integrates Cognito identities with IAM roles to grant temporary, read-only access to specific files or folders in S3. Also, propose a DynamoDB table schema to store metadata for these documents (e.g., file name, upload date, category).\\\\n\\\\nReport back with a detailed plan covering these three areas.\\\",\\n    \\\"recipientAgentID\\\": \\\"6\\\",\\n    \\\"orderSequenceID\\\": \\\"YULAREN-H-1\\\"\\n}\\n###1715014842187-1###\\n###1715014842187-2###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: ORDER\\n\\n{\\n    \\\"orderString\\\": \\\"You are responsible for planning the serverless business logic for the HOA website. Your plan must address the following:\\\\n1.  **Contact Form:** Design the backend for a public contact form. Propose an API Gateway REST API endpoint (e.g., POST /contact) that triggers a Lambda function. This function should validate the input and use Amazon SES to forward the submission to an HOA administrator's email address. Specify the expected JSON payload for the contact form.\\\\n2.  **Code-Free News Updates:** Design the mechanism for a non-technical user to publish news. The plan should use an S3 bucket where the user can upload a simple text or Markdown file. An S3 `s3:ObjectCreated:*` event should trigger a Lambda function. This function will read the new file, process its content, and store it in a DynamoDB table designed to hold news articles. Detail the proposed S3 bucket configuration, the Lambda's logic, and the schema for the news DynamoDB table.\\\\n\\\\nReport back with a comprehensive plan for these serverless components.\\\",\\n    \\\"recipientAgentID\\\": \\\"5\\\",\\n    \\\"orderSequenceID\\\": \\\"YULAREN-MOTTI-1\\\"\\n}\\n###1715014842187-2###\\n###1715014842187-3###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: ORDER\\n\\n{\\n    \\\"orderString\\\": \\\"Your task is to plan the foundational security and permissions architecture for the entire backend, ensuring all services adhere to the principle of least privilege. Your plan should detail:\\\\n1.  **Lambda Execution Roles:** For each Lambda function proposed by the Supervisor of API & Business Logic (contact form, news update), define a specific IAM execution role. List the exact permissions (IAM actions and resources) each role requires to perform its task.\\\\n2.  **API Gateway Permissions:** Specify the permissions model for the API Gateway endpoints. Differentiate between public endpoints (contact form) and potentially authenticated endpoints if any are needed.\\\\n3.  **Authenticated User Permissions:** Define the IAM policy that will be attached to the IAM role for authenticated Cognito users. This policy should grant the necessary read-only permissions for accessing the secure documents in S3 and the news articles in DynamoDB.\\\\n\\\\nProvide a report that lists all required IAM roles and a summary of their associated policies.\\\",\\n    \\\"recipientAgentID\\\": \\\"4\\\",\\n    \\\"orderSequenceID\\\": \\\"YULAREN-C-1\\\"\\n}\\n###1715014842187-3###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Inspection Department, Message Dispatch Service\\nTo: 3\\nType: Approval Request\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"text\\\": \\\"Agent C (4) is requesting approval for call ID SEC-RECRUIT-001 of type RECRUIT. Payload: {\\\\\\\"justification\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"To properly plan the IAM roles and permissions for Lambda functions, I need a specialized agent who understands the intricacies of Lambda execution contexts and can define precise permission boundaries for each function type.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"title\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Attendant of Lambda Security Architecture\\\\\\\"}\\\"\\n}\\n###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"$$$APPROVED$$$\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Inspection Department, Message Dispatch Service\\nTo: 3\\nType: Approval Request\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"text\\\": \\\"Agent Motti (5) is requesting approval for call ID recruit-api-attendant-1 of type RECRUIT. Payload: {\\\\\\\"justification\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"To plan the serverless backend for the public contact form, including the API Gateway endpoint, Lambda function logic, and SES integration, as per Director Yularen's orders (YULAREN-MOTTI-1).\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"title\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Attendant of API and Messaging\\\\\\\"}\\\"\\n}\\n###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"$$$APPROVED$$$\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Inspection Department, Message Dispatch Service\\nTo: 3\\nType: Approval Request\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"text\\\": \\\"Agent Motti (5) is requesting approval for call ID recruit-content-attendant-1 of type RECRUIT. Payload: {\\\\\\\"justification\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"To plan the code-free news update pipeline using S3 for uploads, Lambda for processing, and DynamoDB for storage, as per Director Yularen's orders (YULAREN-MOTTI-1).\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"title\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Attendant of Content Pipelines\\\\\\\"}\\\"\\n}\\n###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"$$$APPROVED$$$\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-22T00:47:59.007Z###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Operations Department, System Call Directorate\\nTo: 3\\nType: Call Results\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"result\\\": \\\"{\\\\n  \\\\\\\"results\\\\\\\": [\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"1715014842187-1\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"details\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Report for order YULAREN-H-1 from agent 6: Supervisor-rank Agent H – Response to Order ID YULAREN-H-1\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n────────────────────────────────────────────\\\\\\\\nDETAILED PLAN: IDENTITY MANAGEMENT & SECURE DATA STORAGE\\\\\\\\n────────────────────────────────────────────\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n1. USER AUTHENTICATION (Amazon Cognito User Pool)\\\\\\\\n-------------------------------------------------\\\\\\\\n1.1  User Pool Name:  HOA_Residents_Prod  (stage-specific suffixes allowed)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n1.2  Sign-in Options\\\\\\\\n     • Username attribute:  email (case-insensitive) – used as primary username\\\\\\\\n     • Auto-verified attributes: email  (SES-verified domain or default Amazon domain)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n1.3  Required / Custom Attributes\\\\\\\\n     • email              (standard, required)\\\\\\\\n     • name               (standard, required)\\\\\\\\n     • addressLine1       (custom:string, max 128, required)         – street address\\\\\\\\n     • unitNumber         (custom:string, max 16, optional)          – apt / unit #\\\\\\\\n     • residencyStatus    (custom:string, \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"owner\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"|\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"renter\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", required)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n1.4  Password Policy\\\\\\\\n     • Minimum length……………… 12 characters\\\\\\\\n     • Require:   ≥1 uppercase, ≥1 lowercase, ≥1 number, ≥1 symbol\\\\\\\\n     • Prevent password reuse (last 3) & check against compromised passwords (Advanced Security)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n1.5  Multi-Factor Authentication (MFA)\\\\\\\\n     • MFA configuration……  ON and ENFORCED for all users after first login\\\\\\\\n     • Preferred method……  TOTP software token (Authenticator apps)\\\\\\\\n     • SMS MFA………………… Enabled as fallback (SES-SMS sandbox exit required)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n1.6  User Pool Security Settings\\\\\\\\n     • Advanced Security………………  PROTECT mode (adaptive risk, compromised credentials checks)\\\\\\\\n     • Account recovery………………  Verified email only\\\\\\\\n     • Token expiration………………   ID/Access 60 min; Refresh 30 days\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n1.7  Groups & Roles\\\\\\\\n     • HOA_Admins      – board members / content uploaders\\\\\\\\n     • HOA_Residents   – default authenticated residents (read-only docs)\\\\\\\\n     • Future groups (e.g., Committee_XXX) allowed\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n1.8  Triggers (Lambdas)\\\\\\\\n     • Post-confirmation – add user to HOA_Residents automatically\\\\\\\\n     • Pre-token-generation – inject custom claims (groups, address) for downstream access logic\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n2. SECURE DOCUMENT STORAGE (Amazon S3)\\\\\\\\n--------------------------------------\\\\\\\\n2.1  Bucket Design\\\\\\\\n     • Primary bucket……  hoa-documents-prod  (private)\\\\\\\\n     • Folders (prefixes):\\\\\\\\n         /meeting-minutes/YYYY/\\\\\\\\n         /financial-reports/YYYY/\\\\\\\\n         /policies/\\\\\\\\n         /misc/\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n2.2  Security Controls\\\\\\\\n     • Block *all* public access (bucket setting)\\\\\\\\n     • Default encryption – SSE-KMS with a CMK   alias/hoa-docs-key\\\\\\\\n         – Key policy limits decrypt to specific IAM roles only\\\\\\\\n     • Bucket policy denies all actions unless:\\\\\\\\n         aws:PrincipalArn matches HOA service roles\\\\\\\\n         or aws:userid matches IAM role session names issued by Cognito Identity Pool\\\\\\\\n     • Versioning – ENABLED (supports audit & rollback)\\\\\\\\n     • Object Ownership – Bucket owner enforced (prevents ACL misuse)\\\\\\\\n     • Server access logging – ENABLED to separate log bucket  hoa-logs-prod\\\\\\\\n     • Lifecycle rules\\\\\\\\n         • Abort multipart uploads after 7 days\\\\\\\\n         • Transition **non-current versions** → Glacier Deep Archive after 2 years\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n2.3  Upload Workflow\\\\\\\\n     • Only users in HOA_Admins assume IAM role  HOAAdminUploadRole (via Cognito or AWS SSO) with s3:PutObject permission restricted to bucket\\\\\\\\n     • Lambda function `DocumentMetadataWriter` writes DynamoDB metadata (see 3.4) upon successful upload (S3 Event → Lambda)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n3. DATA ACCESS CONTROL (Integration of Cognito, IAM, S3, DynamoDB)\\\\\\\\n-------------------------------------------------------------------\\\\\\\\n3.1  Identity Federation (Cognito Identity Pool)\\\\\\\\n     • Identity Pool name……  HOA_Identity_Pool\\\\\\\\n     • Authentication provider… the User Pool above\\\\\\\\n     • Role Mapping……………  Token-based.  Cognito group → IAM role:\\\\\\\\n         – HOA_Residents   → HOAResidentReadOnlyRole\\\\\\\\n         – HOA_Admins      → HOAAdminUploadRole (superset)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n3.2  IAM Roles & Policies\\\\\\\\n     a) HOAResidentReadOnlyRole\\\\\\\\n        • Trust:  cognito-identity.amazonaws.com (for authenticated identities only)\\\\\\\\n        • Permissions:\\\\\\\\n            - s3:GetObject on  arn:aws:s3:::hoa-documents-prod/*\\\\\\\\n              Condition:  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"s3:prefix\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" matches keys returned by the access Lambda (see 3.3)\\\\\\\\n            - dynamodb:GetItem / Query on table HOA_Documents (index by Category)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n     b) HOAAdminUploadRole  (inherits read-only + PutObject rights; separate policy)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n3.3  Secure Retrieval Flow (Web or Mobile Client)\\\\\\\\n     1. User authenticates with Cognito User Pool (MFA enforced) → receives ID/Access tokens.\\\\\\\\n     2. Client exchanges tokens with Cognito Identity Pool → STS credentials for HOAResidentReadOnlyRole.\\\\\\\\n     3. Application calls API Gateway endpoint  /documents?category=financial (signed with SigV4 using temporary creds).\\\\\\\\n     4. Lambda `GetPresignedURL` (behind API GW):\\\\\\\\n        • Verifies caller’s JWT claims/groups.\\\\\\\\n        • Queries DynamoDB by Category (or DocumentID) to fetch S3Key.\\\\\\\\n        • Optional: secondary authorization check (address, committee, etc.).\\\\\\\\n        • Generates S3 pre-signed GET URL (valid 300 s) and returns to client.\\\\\\\\n     5. Client downloads file directly from S3 via pre-signed URL.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n   Advantages: No public S3 access, least-privilege; URLs expire; full audit via CloudTrail.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n3.4  Document Metadata Store (Amazon DynamoDB)\\\\\\\\n     • Table Name………… HOA_Documents\\\\\\\\n     • Primary Key………  DocumentID (string, UUID)\\\\\\\\n     • Sort Key……………  Category  (string)   – enables category queries\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n     Attributes:\\\\\\\\n       - S3Key           (string)  – full object key in bucket\\\\\\\\n       - FileName        (string)\\\\\\\\n       - UploadDate      (string, ISO-8601)\\\\\\\\n       - Year            (number) – GSI partition key for yearly views\\\\\\\\n       - AllowedGroups   (list<string>)  e.g., [\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"HOA_Residents\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"], [\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Finance_Committee\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"]\\\\\\\\n       - UploaderUserID  (string) – sub from Cognito token\\\\\\\\n       - Version         (number)\\\\\\\\n       - Description     (string)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n     GSIs:\\\\\\\\n       • GSI1  PK: Category  SK: UploadDate  (descending sort for recent files)\\\\\\\\n       • GSI2  PK: Year      SK: Category    (yearly reports)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n     Security:\\\\\\\\n       • IAM condition keys restrict Write/Delete to HOAAdminUploadRole.\\\\\\\\n       • Streams:  NEW_IMAGE → CloudWatch Logs (audit) or EventBridge for downstream indexing.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n────────────────────────────────────────────\\\\\\\\nCOST & SECURITY NOTES\\\\\\\\n────────────────────────────────────────────\\\\\\\\n• All components are serverless (Cognito, S3, DynamoDB, Lambda) → pay-per-use and minimal ops.\\\\\\\\n• KMS CMK adds $1/mo + request fees but mandatory for compliance.\\\\\\\\n• Advanced Security Mode in Cognito incurs additional cost (~$0.005 per MAU) but protects against credential stuffing.\\\\\\\\n• No resource is publicly accessible; access is scoped, logged, and auditable (CloudTrail + S3 access logs).\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n────────────────────────────────────────────\\\\\\\\nNEXT STEPS (for Execution Phase planning)\\\\\\\\n────────────────────────────────────────────\\\\\\\\n1. Create CMK, S3 buckets, logging bucket.\\\\\\\\n2. Provision Cognito User Pool & groups, configure SES & SMS.\\\\\\\\n3. Create Identity Pool & IAM roles/policies.\\\\\\\\n4. Deploy DynamoDB table and Lambda functions (triggers + presign URL handler).\\\\\\\\n5. Set up API Gateway endpoints and Integrations.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nAll steps will be codified into a DEP when requested.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n–End of report–\\\\\\\"\\\\n    },\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"1715014842187-2\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"details\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Report for order YULAREN-MOTTI-1 from agent 5: To Director Yularen,\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nIn response to your order (YULAREN-MOTTI-1), I have completed the planning for the serverless business logic for the HOA website. My Attendants have provided detailed component plans, which I have synthesized into the following comprehensive strategy.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nThis plan is divided into two parts, addressing each of the core requirements.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n--- PART 1: CONTACT FORM BACKEND ---\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nThis section details the design for a public contact form that forwards submissions to an HOA administrator via email.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n1.  **API Gateway Endpoint:**\\\\\\\\n    *   **API Type:** REST API.\\\\\\\\n    *   **Resource Path:** `/contact`\\\\\\\\n    *   **Method:** `POST`\\\\\\\\n    *   **Integration:** The endpoint will have a Lambda Proxy integration with the `ContactFormHandler` function.\\\\\\\\n    *   **Security:** The endpoint will be public but will have throttling enabled to prevent abuse. CORS will be configured to allow requests from the website's domain.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n2.  **Lambda Function (`ContactFormHandler`):\\\\\\\\n    *   **Runtime:** Python 3.11.\\\\\\\\n    *   **Trigger:** API Gateway `POST /contact` requests.\\\\\\\\n    *   **Core Logic:**\\\\\\\\n        1.  Receives and parses the JSON payload from the request body.\\\\\\\\n        2.  Performs validation on the input fields (`name`, `email`, `message`).\\\\\\\\n        3.  If validation passes, it uses the Amazon SES SDK to construct and send an email containing the form data to a pre-configured administrator email address.\\\\\\\\n        4.  Returns an HTTP 200 success response.\\\\\\\\n    *   **IAM Role Permissions:** The function's execution role will require `ses:SendEmail` permissions and standard CloudWatch logging permissions.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n3.  **Expected JSON Payload (POST to `/contact`):\\\\\\\\n    ```json\\\\\\\\n    {\\\\\\\\n      \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"name\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"string (1-100 chars)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n      \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"email\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"string (valid email format)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n      \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"message\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"string (1-2000 chars)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n    }\\\\\\\\n    ```\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n--- PART 2: CODE-FREE NEWS UPDATE SYSTEM ---\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nThis section details the mechanism allowing a non-technical user to publish news articles by simply uploading a file.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n1.  **S3 Upload Bucket (`hoa-news-uploads-bucket`):\\\\\\\\n    *   **Purpose:** A private S3 bucket will be created as the designated drop zone for news articles.\\\\\\\\n    *   **Configuration:** All public access will be blocked. Authorized users will be granted specific IAM permissions to upload files.\\\\\\\\n    *   **Workflow:** A user uploads a `.txt` or `.md` file. The first line is treated as the article title, and the rest of the file is the content.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n2.  **S3 Event Trigger & Lambda (`ProcessNewsArticleFunction`):\\\\\\\\n    *   **Trigger:** An S3 event notification for `s3:ObjectCreated:*` will be configured on the bucket, filtered for `.txt` and `.md` suffixes.\\\\\\\\n    *   **Lambda Function (`ProcessNewsArticleFunction`):**\\\\\\\\n        *   **Runtime:** Python 3.11.\\\\\\\\n        *   **Core Logic:**\\\\\\\\n            1.  Triggered by the S3 event, receiving the file's bucket and key.\\\\\\\\n            2.  Uses the S3 SDK to read the content of the newly uploaded file.\\\\\\\\n            3.  Parses the file into a title and content.\\\\\\\\n            4.  Generates a unique `articleID` (UUID) and a `creationDate` timestamp.\\\\\\\\n            5.  Uses the DynamoDB SDK to save the structured data as a new item in the news table.\\\\\\\\n        *   **IAM Role Permissions:** The function's role requires `s3:GetObject` on the uploads bucket and `dynamodb:PutItem` on the news table, plus logging permissions.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n3.  **DynamoDB News Table (`HOA_News_Articles`):\\\\\\\\n    *   **Purpose:** To durably store and serve news articles to the frontend.\\\\\\\\n    *   **Schema:**\\\\\\\\n        *   **Partition Key:** `articleID` (String) - A unique UUID.\\\\\\\\n        *   **Attributes:**\\\\\\\\n            *   `title` (String)\\\\\\\\n            *   `content` (String)\\\\\\\\n            *   `creationDate` (String) - An ISO 8601 timestamp for chronological sorting.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nThis comprehensive plan provides a secure, scalable, and cost-effective serverless solution that meets all specified requirements. The components are designed to be deployed deterministically during the Execution phase. I await your review and further instructions.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nEnd of report.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    },\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"1715014842187-3\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"details\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Report for order YULAREN-C-1 from agent 4: Security Architecture Plan for HOA Website Backend\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n## 1. Lambda Execution Roles\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n### A. Contact Form Handler Lambda\\\\\\\\n**Role Name:** HOAContactFormLambdaRole\\\\\\\\n**Required Permissions:**\\\\\\\\n- ses:SendEmail (Resource: arn:aws:ses:*:*:identity/*)\\\\\\\\n- logs:CreateLogGroup (Resource: arn:aws:logs:*:*:*)\\\\\\\\n- logs:CreateLogStream (Resource: arn:aws:logs:*:*:*)\\\\\\\\n- logs:PutLogEvents (Resource: arn:aws:logs:*:*:*)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n### B. News Update Lambda\\\\\\\\n**Role Name:** HOANewsUpdateLambdaRole\\\\\\\\n**Required Permissions:**\\\\\\\\n- s3:GetObject (Resource: arn:aws:s3:::hoa-news-upload-bucket/*)\\\\\\\\n- s3:DeleteObject (Resource: arn:aws:s3:::hoa-news-upload-bucket/*)\\\\\\\\n- dynamodb:PutItem (Resource: arn:aws:dynamodb:*:*:table/HOA_NewsArticles)\\\\\\\\n- dynamodb:UpdateItem (Resource: arn:aws:dynamodb:*:*:table/HOA_NewsArticles)\\\\\\\\n- logs:CreateLogGroup (Resource: arn:aws:logs:*:*:*)\\\\\\\\n- logs:CreateLogStream (Resource: arn:aws:logs:*:*:*)\\\\\\\\n- logs:PutLogEvents (Resource: arn:aws:logs:*:*:*)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n## 2. API Gateway Permissions\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n### A. Public Endpoints\\\\\\\\n**Contact Form Endpoint (/contact)**\\\\\\\\n- Authentication: None required\\\\\\\\n- CORS: Enabled for HOA website domain\\\\\\\\n- Throttling: 10 requests per second per IP\\\\\\\\n- Integration: Lambda proxy integration with HOAContactFormLambdaRole\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n### B. Authenticated Endpoints (if needed for future expansion)\\\\\\\\n**Reserved for future authenticated API endpoints**\\\\\\\\n- Authenti